# Frontend Security Standards

- Never expose secrets in frontend code.
- Treat all frontend data as untrusted.
- Avoid dangerouslySetInnerHTML unless sanitized.

## JWT and authentication

- Do not expose JWT tokens in logs or URLs.
- Handle 401 Unauthorized properly.
- Login screens must avoid leaking security details.

## Sensitive data

- Avoid storing sensitive information insecurely.
- Do not expose backend internals to users.
- Avoid leaking stack traces or technical details.

## Input handling

- Validate and sanitize user input where appropriate.